{"name":"Cabin Fever","hex":"#5e5349","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cabin fever","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A condition of restlessness and irritability caused by being in a confined space.","Typhus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabin_fever"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cabin Fever (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Cabin Fever (1990) is a novel by Australian writer Elizabeth Jolley. It was originally published by Viking in Australia in 1990."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Cabin_Fever_%28novel%29_book_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabin_Fever_(novel)","wikidata":"Q123757832"},{"title":"Cabin Fever (2002 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cabin Fever is a 2002 American comedy horror film, co-written and directed by Eli Roth in his directorial debut. It follows a group of college students who rent a cabin in the woods, where they unwittingly come in contact with an unknown flesh-eating disease. It stars Rider Strong, Jordan Ladd, James DeBello, Cerina Vincent, Joey Kern, and Giuseppe Andrews."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Movie_poster_cabin_fever.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabin_Fever_(2002_film)","wikidata":"Q1024838"},{"title":"Cabin fever","blocks":[{"text":"Cabin fever is the distressing irritability or restlessness experienced when a person, or group, is stuck at an isolated location or in confined quarters for an extended time. A person may be referred to as stir-crazy, derived from the use of stir meaning \"prison\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/CABIN%2C_INTERIOR%2C_LOOKING_SOUTHWEST_-_Roy_Fure%27s_Trapping_Cabin%2C_King_Salmon%2C_Bristol_Bay_Borough%2C_AK_HABS_AK%2C4-KISAL.V%2C1-5.tif/lossy-page1-330px-CABIN%2C_INTERIOR%2C_LOOKING_SOUTHW